## Context

The 254 extracted documents (13,092 lines, 253 snapshots; `docs/jetp-requirements.md` DA2) are the only oracle
the pipeline has. Replaying them through the pipeline is what makes "works on
all we hold" a testable claim, and it is the byte-invariance property the
author wanted for the robust version. It binds parsers and the writer; an LLM
read is not byte-reproducible, so lines that came from a hand or LLM read are
compared, not regenerated (list them in the report).

Of the 13,092 lines, 10,452 are comparator records (CRS, IATI and World
Bank) in the 91 snapshots kept outside the document store (requirements
DA2). They are replayed at M2 by the ingestion run of
`docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 6.2 under its count control, not by a parser
(extraction § 13: "the held comparator snapshots replayed under the count
control"). This is phase M2.1 of [[1500]]: the deterministic lane, whose
oracle already exists, run before any LLM reads anything.

## Work

- For each extracted document, run the pipeline from its snapshot and compare
  to the committed lines and `line-fields/` row by row.
- Classify every difference: the pipeline is wrong, the committed line is
  wrong (then a ticket, under the severity floor), or the difference is
  legitimate and explained.
- Report which documents replay exactly, which differ, which cannot be
  regenerated (hand-read), by country and type.
- Comparator snapshots: an ingestion run per snapshot states the records
  read, the declared fields and the counts rejected, and compares the number
  read with the number the service or file states, else the count recorded
  when the snapshot was first read; a mismatch fails that snapshot and
  admits nothing from it (extraction § 6.2).
- Positive control: a deliberately altered snapshot or line must make the
  harness fail.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every one of the 254 documents is reported: replays exactly, differs (explained), or not regenerable (named)
- [ ] The comparator snapshots (81 CRS, 4 IATI, 6 World Bank and ledger exports) are replayed by an ingestion run under the count control of extraction § 6.2; a red test with one record removed fails the snapshot and admits nothing from it
- [ ] Pilot on a stratified sample (country × format, comparator and document-store snapshots both represented, size stated) passes a quality check by a cross-model checker, findings recorded here, before the full replay (pilot rule, [[1500]])
- [ ] The positive control fires
- [ ] The harness runs in `make check-domain-jetp` or is named as a slow gate, with its data requirement stated (needs the snapshot bytes: padme)
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check` and `make lint` pass
